>> *Some* of these effects are covered in various of the *-343.txt
>> spoilers as pertinent to their topics.
>
> Which? Is there some other spoiler that has the info?

armr-343.txt:

If armor is enchanted above +3 (+5 for cornuthaums if you are a Wizard
or for elven armor), then there is a chance of it being destroyed if it
is enchanted further.

weap-343.txt:

[multishot]
  +   1 if you are an elf firing elven arrows from an elven bow.
  +   1 if you are an orc firing orcish arrows from an orcish bow.

[to-hit]
+   1 if you are an elf or Samurai wielding any bow and shooting any arrow.
    This bonus is 2 when an elf uses an elven bow or a Samurai uses a yumi.

[damage]
+   1 if you're a Samurai using ya with a yumi, or are an elf using elven
    arrows with an elven bow. Polymorph doesn't count.

Other than these, the only differences are initial knowledge (you
start recognising all your own racial gear); the base values as listed
in the spoilers; and the ability of hobbits to wear elven armour
regardless of size. I don't immediately see anything else.

